    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "Are you kidding ??? What the **** are you talking about man ?\n\nHear
    me out: If everything were legal, nothing would be illegal.\nIf nothing were
    illegal, nothing would be funny.\nIf nothing were funny, we would be playing
    regular chess.\n\nAnarchy can only exist in a world where rules exist just long
    enough\nfor us to violate them in creative, unhinged ways.\n\nLast time we didn't
    play by the rules, something bad happened.  \nGoogle the en passant ban of 1984.
    Worst year to be alive.\n\nBecause the mods are going to ban me, I proposed a
    few new rules: \n\n1.1 En passant is considered forced move. However, a player
    may choose not to play en passant when the opportunity arrives, but this will
    result in their PiPi getting bricked. So while en passant is technically not
    forced, any player that understands en passant and values his PiPi will not decline
    it.\nPipi gambit? Are you kidding ??? What the **** are you talking about man
    ?\r\n\r\n1.2 There is no agreed upon penalty for women that decline en passant,
    mostly because they shouldn\u2019t play Chess, you know. They're like beginners.
    They lose every single game against a man. There isn't a woman player in the
    world I can't give knook-odds to and still beat.\r\n\r\n2.1 Anarchy fairy Chess
    pieces will usually involve a combination of different pieces (hybrids) ex: Knook
    as a combination of knight and rook,\r\n\r\n2.2 pieces of mixed color (traitor
    pieces) ex: Traitor Rook as a Rook that can be moved by and captured by any player
    with the colors it has,\r\n\r\n2.3 pieces with part of them cut off, limiting
    them to certain directions (handicapped pieces) ex: Look as a Rook that can only
    move left, left meaning from the h file to the a file,\r\n\r\n2.4 or pieces rotated
    to change direction (rotated pieces) ex: Tilted Bishop that moves just as a rook
    does.\r\n\r\n3. The King cannot move to a c2 square.\r\n\r\n4.1 A double check
    (when 2 pieces attack the King) is considered a loss by checkmate for the player
    receiving the double check.\r\n\r\n4.2 A player that checkmates by double check
    may declare \u201Cwe\u2019re having pasta for dinner,\u201D and both players
    must eat pasta once it is the appropriate time to have dinner.\r\n\r\n4.3 A player
    that is in a position in which their king is checked by more than 2 pieces, such
    as a triple check, will lose the game and die in real life.\r\n\r\n5. c4 is explosive."
