MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 579860460}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: 4b1075986e31e684892255986fb0020c, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 24
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 224
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "In the year 1984, George Orwell warned us of a future ruled by obedience,
    surveillance, and a total extinction of joy. Back then, no one realized that
    the prophecy wasn\u2019t about governments, politics, or society. No, Orwell
    wrote about something far worse. Something far more terrifying.\n\nHe wrote about
    standard chess.\n\"Big Brother is watching you\"\n\nA universe where bishops
    politely stay on diagonals, pawns march only forward like good little soldiers,
    and the en passant square is determined by\u2014shudders\u2014logic. A place
    where rooks don\u2019t teleport, knights don\u2019t commit war crimes, and kings
    aren\u2019t allowed to sprint across the board like they forgot to turn off the
    oven.\n\nThis is the world Jessica wants.\n\nAnd this is the world we reject.\n\nFuck
    you J*ssica!\n\nShe says:\n\u201CEn passant only works under specific conditions.\u201D\n\nWe
    say:\n\u201CGoogle says otherwise.\u201D\n\n\nEvery empire falls.\nRome fell.\nThe
    Soviet Union fell.\nMy rating fell to 410 after playing Bongcloud for science."
