--- !u!114 &1586744903
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1586744901}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: 4b1075986e31e684892255986fb0020c, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 24
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 224
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "Orwell taught us that when a system becomes too rigid, too restrictive,
    too absolute\u2026 the only path to truth is rebellion.\n\nThus emerges Anarchy
    Chess.\n\nA philosophy.\nA movement.\nA revolution of the board.\n\nHere, the
    king can double jump.\nHere, pawns can unionize.\nHere, the knight can roll a
    d20 to decide its next square.\nHere, castling is performed by yeeting the king
    over the rook like a medieval Olympic sport.\n\nHere, rules aren\u2019t rules\u2014just
    suggestions.\n\nBecause in the year of 1984, the only way to fight oppression
    is with overwhelming, unregulated high-intensity chess.\n\nFreedom is Illegal.\nIllegal
    is Allowed.\nAnd Allowed is Mandatory.\n\nLiberte\nEgalite\nFraternite\n\nAlso,
    Wilhelm Steinitz is the first and only true world chess champion and as such
    the owner of chess. After his death, chess passed into the possession of his
    homeland Austria-Hungary. After the Anschluss, it was stolen by the Germans and
    kept under wraps. Now, 80 years after the end of the Third Reich, the copyrights
    expired. Thus, it has only now been revealed that Anarchy Chess is German.\nThis
    historical distortion is unbearable. Now they're even conjuring up fictional
    Austrians just to distract from the performance of Garryschach and Gavin from
    third grade.\r\nJessica Steinitz is not welcome here.\n"
